Town phase 2: the text-size stills are up, for the director (branch stills/town-phase2, 5 images and a README).

Before (a picture for every size), new with one size (a tag made at 12 px, a home's name at 20, scaled by the GPU), new with two sizes
(9 and 12; 14 and 20): the names and tags at every zoom step, a phone and a computer.
- Phone (the canvas at 2x): the three can't be told apart.
- Computer at 1x: the smallest tags (8 px) are a touch softer with one size; two sizes doesn't improve them (9 scaled to 8 is as soft
  as 12 scaled to 8). The names read the same. `text-smallest-tags-computer-7x.png` is that hardest case, 7 times over.

So the branch is built with one size (the brief's default) and I'm going on with the rest. If you'd rather have two sizes it's one line
each in packages/app/src/town/feel.ts (`tagPicSizes: [9, 12]`, `namePicSizes: [14, 20]`): nothing else changes. Text pixels on the
phone: 8.67 M before, 1.29 M with one size.
